  <section id="sect-00004">
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <para id="para-00075">Solve the systems of equations by substitution.</para>
      <para id="para-00076">
            \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x\;+\;y\;=\;-4\\\;3x\;-\;2y\;=\;-6\end{array}\right.\)</para>
          </note>
  </section>

  <section id="sect-00005">
    <title>Additional Resources</title>

    <section id="sect-00006">
      <title>Reinforcing the Substitution Method</title>
      <para id="para-00077">Solve the system by substitution:</para>

      <!--BEGIN
      SYSTEM OF EQUATIONS-->

      <para id="para-00078">\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;+\;2y\;=\;4\\6x\;+\;-y\;=\;8\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      <!--END
      SYSTEM OF EQUATIONS -->
      <para id="para-00079">We need to solve one equation for one variable. We will solve the first equation for
        \(y\).</para>
      <!--BEGIN
      STEPS-->

        <para id="para-00080"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Solve the first equation for \(y\).</para>
        <!--BEGIN
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
     <para id="para-00081">\(\begin{array}{rcl}
        4x+2y&amp;=&amp;4 \\2y&amp;=&amp;-4x+4 \\y&amp;=&amp;-2x+2 \\ \end{array}\)</para>
        <!--END
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->

   <para id="para-00082"><emphasis>Step
        2 -</emphasis> Substitute \(−2x+2\) for \(y\) in the second equation.</para>
        <!--BEGIN
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
   <para id="para-00083">\(\begin{array}{rcl}
        6x-y&amp;=&amp;8 \\6x-(-2x+2)&amp;=&amp;8 \\ \end{array}\)</para>
        <!--END
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->

	<para id="para-00084"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis>
        Solve the equation for \(x\).</para>
        <!--BEGIN
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  <para id="para-00085">\(\begin{array}{rcl} 6x-(-2x+2)&amp;=&amp;8
        \\6x+2x-2&amp;=&amp;8 \\8x-2&amp;=&amp;8 \\8x&amp;=&amp;10 \\x&amp;=&amp;\frac{10}{8}
        \\x&amp;=&amp;\frac54 \\ \end{array}\)</para>
        <!--END
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->

	<para id="para-00086"><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Substitute
        \(x=\frac54\) into \(4x+2y=4\) to find \(y\).</para>
        <!--BEGIN
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  <para id="para-00087">\(\begin{array}{rcl}
        4x+2y&amp;=&amp;4 \\ 4(\frac54)+2y&amp;=&amp;4 \\5+2y&amp;=&amp;4 \\2y&amp;=&amp;-1
        \\y&amp;=&amp;\frac{-1}{2} \\ \end{array}\)</para>
        <!--END
        ALIGN TO EQUALS -->

	<para id="para-00088"><emphasis>Step 5 -</emphasis> Check
        the ordered pair. \((\frac54,\frac{-1}{2})\) in both equations.</para>
        <!--BEGIN
        SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS-->
  <para id="para-00089">\(\begin{array}{rr}
          &amp; 6x-y=8\\   &amp; 6(\frac54)-(-\frac12)\overset?=8\\ 4x+2y=4 &amp;
        \frac{30}{4}-(-\frac12)\overset?=8\\ 4(-\frac12)+2(\frac54)\overset?=4 &amp;
        \frac{15}{2}-(-\frac12)\overset?=8\\ 5-1\overset?=4 &amp; \frac{15}{2}+\frac12\overset?=8 \\
        4=4\checkmark &amp; 8=8\checkmark\\ \end{array}\)</para>
        <!--END
        SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS -->

      <!-- END STEPS -->

      <note class="try look-at-me" id="note-00002">
      <title>Try It: Reinforcing the Substitution Method</title>

      <!--Q#-->
        <exercise id="exer-00006">
          <problem id="prob-00017">

            <para id="para-00090">Solve the system by substitution:</para>
            <!--BEGIN
            SYSTEM OF EQUATIONS-->
            <para id="para-00091">\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x\;-\;4y\;=\;-4\\-3x\;+\;4y\;=\;0\end{array}\right.\)</para>
            <!--END
            SYSTEM OF EQUATIONS -->
            <para id="para-00092">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
              compare your work.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00017">
            <para id="para-00093">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>

            <para id="para-00094"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Solve the first equation for \( x \) to isolate a
              variable.</para>

            <para id="para-00095">
              \(\begin{array}{rcl}\;\;x\;-\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\\x\;-\;4y\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}4}{\style{color:red}y}\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}4}{\style{color:red}y}\\x\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\;+\;4y\end{array}\)</para>

            <para id="para-00096"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Replace the \(x\) in the second equation with the
              expression \( -4 + 4y \).</para>

            <para id="para-00097">
              \(\begin{array}{rcl}-3x\;+\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0\\-3{\style{color:red}(}{\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}4}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}4}{\style{color:red}y}{\style{color:red})}\;+\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0\end{array}\)</para>

            <para id="para-00098"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Solve the equation with just one variable.</para>

            <para id="para-00099">
              \(\begin{array}{rcl}-3(-4\;+\;4y)\;+\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0\\12 -
              12y\;+\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;0\\-8y\;&amp;=&amp;\;-12\\y\;&amp;=&amp;\;\;\frac32\end{array}\)</para>

            <para id="para-00100"><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Use the first equation and replace \(y\) with
              \(\frac32\).</para>

            <para id="para-00101">
              \(\begin{array}{rcl}x\;-\;4y\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\\x\;-\;4(\frac32)\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\\x\;-\;6\;&amp;=&amp;\;-4\\x\;&amp;=&amp;\;2\end{array}\)</para>

            <para id="para-00102"><emphasis>Step 5 -</emphasis> The ordered pair is \((x, y)\).</para>

            <para id="para-00103"> \((2,\frac32)\)</para>

            <para id="para-00104"><emphasis>Step 6 -</emphasis> Substitute \( x=6 \), \( y=1 \) to check the
              solution in both equations.</para>

            <para id="para-00105">
              \(\begin{array}{r}x\;-\;4y\;=\;-4\\\;{\style{color:red}(}{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red})}\;-\;4{\style{color:red}(}\frac{\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red})}\stackrel{?}{=}-4\\\;2\;-\;6\stackrel{?}{=}-4\\-4\;=\;-4\;{\style{color:red}✔}\end{array}\)</para>

            <para id="para-00106">
              \(\begin{array}{r}-3x\;+\;4y\;=\;0\\\;-3{\style{color:red}(}{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red})}\;-\;4{\style{color:red}(}\frac{\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}2}{\style{color:red})}\stackrel{?}{=}0\\\;-6\;+\;6\stackrel{?}{=}0\\0\;=\;0\;{\style{color:red}✔}\end{array}\)
  </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note><!--Interaction
      End -->

      <!-- END TRY IT -->
    </section>
  </section>
  </content>
